<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/"
      xmlns:its="http://www.w3.org/2005/11/its"
      type="topic" style="task"
      id="pref-extensions">

  <info>
    <link type="guide" xref="index#pref"/>
    <revision pkgversion="51.1" date="2026-10-15" status="candidate"/>

    <include href="legal.xml" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"/>

    <desc>How to add, turn on, and remove browser extensions.</desc>
  </info>

  <title>Extensions</title>

  <p><app>SparkyBin Browser</app> can run web extensions written for Mozilla
  Firefox. Extensions can read and change the pages you visit, so only install
  extensions that you trust.</p>

  <note style="important">
    <p>Extensions are enabled by default. An extension that you turn on can read
    and change the pages you visit, so only add extensions from sources you
    trust, and remove any that you no longer use.</p>
  </note>

  <section id="install">
    <title>Install an extension</title>

    <steps>
      <item>
        <p>Download the extension's <file>.xpi</file> file. To find extensions,
        visit <link href="https://addons.mozilla.org">addons.mozilla.org</link>.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and
        select <guiseq><gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui><gui style="tab">Extensions</gui></guiseq>.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>Press <gui style="menuitem">Add New Extension</gui> and choose the
        file that you downloaded.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>Switch the extension on to start using it.</p>
      </item>
    </steps>
  </section>

  <section id="enable">
    <title>Turn an extension on or off</title>

    <steps>
      <item>
        <p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and
        select <guiseq><gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui><gui style="tab">Extensions</gui></guiseq>.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>Switch the extension off to stop it from changing the pages that you
        visit, or on to use it again.</p>
      </item>
    </steps>

    <p>To stop extensions from running at all, switch
    <gui>Enable WebExtensions</gui> off. The <gui>Extensions</gui> page is then
    removed from the <gui>Preferences</gui>.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="remove">
    <title>Remove an extension</title>

    <steps>
      <item>
        <p>Press the menu button in the top-right corner of the window and
        select <guiseq><gui style="menuitem">Preferences</gui><gui style="tab">Extensions</gui></guiseq>.</p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>Select the extension, then press
        <gui style="menuitem">Remove Extension…</gui>.</p>
      </item>
    </steps>
  </section>

  <note style="tip">
    <p>Not every Firefox extension is supported. Extensions that depend on parts
    of the extension API which <app>SparkyBin Browser</app> does not implement
    may not work correctly.</p>
  </note>

</page>
